{"name":"Arabian Nights","hex":"#016c84","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["At night (during night-time, especially on a regular basis)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of night"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arabian Nights (1974 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Arabian Nights is a 1974 erotic fantasy comedy anthology film directed by Pier Paolo Pasolini. The film is an adaptation of the ancient Arabic anthology One Thousand and One Nights, also known as The Arabian Nights. It is mostly based on the tale Ali Shar and Zumurrud. It is the last of Pasolini's \"Trilogy of Life\", which began with The Decameron and continued with The Canterbury Tales. The lead was played by young Franco Merli who was discovered for this film by Pasolini. The film is an adaptation of several stories within the original collection but they are presented out of order and without the Scheherazade, Dunyazad and King Shahriyar frame story."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/ArabianKnightsPasolini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_Nights_(1974_film)","wikidata":"Q209737"},{"title":"Arabian Nights (ballet)","blocks":[{"text":"One Thousand and One Nights Arabian Nights is a two-part ballet written in 1979. The music of the ballet was written by Fikret Amirov, and the libretto was written by Magsud and Rustam Ibrahimbeyov based on the fairy tale \" Arabian Nights”. The premiere of the ballet took place in 1979 at the Azerbaijan State Academic Opera and Ballet Theater."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_Nights_(ballet)","wikidata":"Q8479451"},{"title":"One Thousand and One Nights","blocks":[{"text":"One Thousand and One Nights or The Thousand and One Nights is a collection of Middle Eastern folktales compiled in the Arabic language during the Islamic Golden Age. It is often known in English as The Arabian Nights, from the first English-language edition, which rendered the title as The Arabian Nights' Entertainments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/William-Strang-Sindbad-AliBaba-titlepage.JPG/330px-William-Strang-Sindbad-AliBaba-titlepage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Thousand_and_One_Nights","wikidata":"Q8258"},{"title":"Arabian Peninsula","blocks":[{"text":"The Arabian Peninsula, or simply Arabia, is a peninsula in West Asia. It accounts for the majority of the land situated on the Arabian plate. With an area of 3,237,500 km2 (1.25 million mi2), it is the world's largest peninsula—roughly comparable in size to India. Nine countries are located on the Arabian Peninsula: Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, and Yemen, as well as the southern halves of Iraq and Jordan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg/330px-Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_Peninsula","wikidata":"Q31945"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg/250px-Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg/500px-Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg/250px-Historic_Town_of_Zabid-111632.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistoric_Town_of_